WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.732
Android forensics requires careful handling, authorized acquisition, artifact knowledge, timeline correlation, and disciplined interpretation.

2
00:00:09.732 --> 00:00:17.879
The investigator's task is to preserve evidence, understand where artifacts came from, and explain what the findings support.

3
00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:21.651
Strong work begins with authorization and documentation.

4
00:00:21.651 --> 00:00:30.704
Investigators should record device condition, power state, lock state, network considerations, custody, methods, and acquisition scope.

5
00:00:30.704 --> 00:00:38.022
Logical, file system, and cloud or account-based acquisition concepts each provide different views of evidence.

6
00:00:38.022 --> 00:00:42.699
No method should be described as complete without explaining its limits.

7
00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:46.018
Android architecture matters throughout the case.

8
00:00:46.018 --> 00:00:57.108
Version differences, app sandboxing, encryption, scoped storage, Google services, OEM customization, accounts, and sync settings all affect access and interpretation.

9
00:00:57.108 --> 00:01:02.917
App artifacts may be local, cached, synchronized, restored, or generated automatically.

10
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:09.179
Device possession, account activity, and user intent should not be collapsed into the same claim.

11
00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:12.649
Analysis should correlate artifacts across sources.

12
00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:25.021
Communications, browser records, notifications, media, EXIF metadata, location traces, app data, cloud records, network logs, and witness statements can reinforce or challenge each other.

13
00:01:25.021 --> 00:01:28.718
Timestamps need normalization and careful explanation.

14
00:01:28.718 --> 00:01:33.998
Location and activity evidence should be reported with appropriate uncertainty.

15
00:01:33.998 --> 00:01:37.016
The goal is not to extract everything possible.

16
00:01:37.016 --> 00:01:47.879
The goal is to preserve relevant evidence, protect privacy, analyze artifacts responsibly, document uncertainty, and support defensible investigative conclusions.

17
00:01:47.879 --> 00:01:54.669
Good Android forensics is as much about restraint and interpretation as it is about technical collection.
